WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.769
-Our next guest is a talented
actor and musician who is

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:05.137
currently on
his "Mainstream Sellout" tour.

00:00:05.137 --> 00:00:08.641
His new album, "Mainstream
Sellout (Life in Pink Deluxe)"

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.711
is available now. You can also
see his documentary,

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:14.080
"Machine Gun Kelly's
Life in Pink" on Hulu.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.915
Let's take a look.

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:17.683
-This is 112th and Dove.

00:00:17.683 --> 00:00:19.385
We always had these big dreams.

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:21.787
Ladies and gentlemen,
how are y'all feeling?

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:23.722
I like that energy.
[ Laughs ]

00:00:23.722 --> 00:00:26.225
First music video I ever shot
was right there

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:27.760
in front of that ADM Deli.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:30.396
I got a gun pulled on me right
here, and I was like,

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:32.232
"Are you going to do this with
my daughter in the car?"

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:35.601
-Please welcome back to the show
Machine Gun Kelly, everybody.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.270
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:45.712 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:49.415
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:52.618
Welcome back to the show.
How are you?

00:00:52.618 --> 00:00:54.354
-There are censors, right?

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:56.122
-Yeah, yeah.
-I feel like [bleep]

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:57.523
-Oh, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.523 --> 00:00:59.925
Well, I know you did a sold-out
show at MSG last night.

00:00:59.925 --> 00:01:01.293
Congratulations.
-Thanks, thanks.

00:01:01.293 --> 00:01:03.496
-But last time you were here,
you'd just done the VMAs.

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:05.664
You'd hurt your hand at the VMAs

00:01:05.664 --> 00:01:08.434
and you hurt yourself again
last night at MSG.

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:12.338
-Yeah, I almost -- I'm going to
start having doctors around me

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:13.973
every time I see Seth Meyers
on my schedule.

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:16.942
-Yeah, the night before.
So what happened last night?

00:01:16.942 --> 00:01:22.348
-Um, you know, you know when you
clink a champagne glass with

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:23.482
a fork to kind of --

00:01:23.482 --> 00:01:25.084
-To get people's attention
to start a toast?

00:01:25.084 --> 00:01:27.186
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:30.056
-Yeah, I didn't have a fork.
-Okay.

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:32.458
-So I just clinked it
on my head.

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:34.727
-Okay.
-Um...

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.863
-That's a -- You know, they call
that, you know what --

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:38.597
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.597 --> 00:01:40.867
In medicine, they call that
"asking for it."

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:43.769
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.769 --> 00:01:45.804
-Yeah, so I had a serious case
of that last night.

00:01:45.804 --> 00:01:47.907
-Yeah, yeah, you had a serious
case of -- How was it?

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:50.810
How was the show? Must be always
fun to perform in New York City.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.512
-Ow, f-- Um, sorry.

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:55.815
I keep forgetting I have this,
but I'm a hand talker, so I --

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:58.317
-Oh, right. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:58.317 --> 00:02:02.822
-You know, my first music check
was from New York City.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:05.525
It was -- I was the first rapper
to win amateur night

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:07.293
at the Apollo Theater in Harlem.
-Really?

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:09.695
-And it was for $45.
-That's a pretty --

00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:11.297
I mean, it must have felt like
a million dollars at the time.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.967
-Absolutely.
And I never cashed it.

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:15.401
I always just held on to it.

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:19.772
And I think --

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.474
Well, the only thing I said
the whole day was

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:23.276
"We're at the Garden.
We're at the Garden."

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:26.812
And, like, there's obviously --
you know, growing up,

00:02:26.812 --> 00:02:28.915
I watched -- It's funny that
we have a documentary called

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:31.117
"Life in Pink" because we
watched "Fade to Black,"

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:33.519
which was Jay-Z's doc,
so much growing up.

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:37.289
And right before we did the
Garden, we got to -- Yeah.

00:02:37.289 --> 00:02:38.924
-Yeah, the Empire State
Building.

00:02:38.924 --> 00:02:40.860
This was pink last night
in honor of your album.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.095
That's a pretty big deal when

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:43.829
they do the Empire State
Building.

00:02:43.829 --> 00:02:45.664
They decided to do this before
they heard you're the kind of

00:02:45.664 --> 00:02:48.468
guy who smashes a glass
against his own head.

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:51.937
[ Laughter ]
-Thank God I waited.

00:02:51.937 --> 00:02:54.107
-Did you get to go hang out at
the -- Did you get to go

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:55.207
to the Empire State Building
for the lighting?

00:02:55.207 --> 00:02:56.242
-I did, I did.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:57.643
So they took me on a --

00:02:57.643 --> 00:02:59.878
This is where everybody
kind of stops at.

00:02:59.878 --> 00:03:01.714
And then they showed me
a secret ladder

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:03.649
that takes you right there.
-Really?

00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:05.184
-Yeah.
-You were that high?

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:07.653
-Mm-hmm. Thank God I didn't have
a champagne glass up there.

00:03:07.653 --> 00:03:10.222
[ Laughter ]
Excuse me! New York!

00:03:10.222 --> 00:03:12.792
-So I want to ask about
"Mainstream Sellout."

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:15.762
That seems like, I don't know,
a bit of a provocative title.

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:18.497
How did you come up with that
as the title for your album?

00:03:18.497 --> 00:03:21.700
-I think because I was trying to
be provocative.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.503
-Yeah, okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.503 --> 00:03:26.172
So I got it nailed?

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:28.241
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:32.378
-I kind of -- I'm -- I think
it was almost

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:35.715
like I'm just in on the joke.
-Yeah.

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:40.019
-I put an album out prior to
that was really successful

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:44.323
in a genre that wasn't
in the mainstream.

00:03:44.323 --> 00:03:47.426
And, you know, I was known for

00:03:47.426 --> 00:03:49.428
doing a different genre of music
as well.

00:03:49.428 --> 00:03:51.764
So I think it just kind of --

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:53.632
Success breeds hate.

00:03:53.632 --> 00:03:57.937
And I was kind of like...

00:03:57.937 --> 00:04:00.173
"But I'm hilarious, so this is
the title of the new --"

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:01.674
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:04.510
I was -- It was almost like...

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:08.047
You know when you shake hands
with -- when, like, you're

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:09.715
in competition with someone
and you shake hands

00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:12.284
and you smile at them
and you know you won?

00:04:12.284 --> 00:04:14.152
-Yeah, and then you shake it
for a super-long time.

00:04:14.152 --> 00:04:15.788
-But then you just shake it
and you're just like...

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:16.956
-Yeah.
-Yeah, that was me.

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:17.857
-That was you.

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:19.959
-That was me with
all of the hate.

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:20.993
-You're talking about --

00:04:20.993 --> 00:04:22.361
Here is your documentary
that I mentioned.

00:04:22.361 --> 00:04:24.430
We talk about the fact that you
did sort of switch genres

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.933
and the documentary shows
your early roots doing hip-hop.

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:28.667
Then you've got,
you know, pop-punk.

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:30.202
You sort of move into
this different genre.

00:04:30.202 --> 00:04:31.570
Do you feel -- You know, again,

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:32.738
you're still early
in your career.

00:04:32.738 --> 00:04:34.340
Do you think you're going to
drift back

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.542
to different genres,
move on to a new genre?

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:38.544
Do you have any plans or do you
think it just sort of happens

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:40.946
organically when you sit down
to write new music?

00:04:40.946 --> 00:04:42.948
-Well, I did buy an accordion.

00:04:42.948 --> 00:04:44.583
-You did?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:46.419
So...
-I think that's pretty exciting.

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:48.787
You know, Steve Carell plays...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.787 --> 00:04:50.590
Steve Carell plays fife.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.492
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.492 --> 00:04:54.193
And I feel like you get the two.

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:55.694
-Wow.
[ Applause ]

00:04:55.694 --> 00:04:57.363
-I feel like there's no --

00:04:57.363 --> 00:05:00.099
There's no mainstream
accordion-fife duo.

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:03.002
-Mm. Yeah, we're going
underground anyway.

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:06.705
We want to be more of
like a cult band.

00:05:06.705 --> 00:05:08.874
-You got engaged.
-I did.

00:05:08.874 --> 00:05:11.010
-You and your fiancée,
Megan Fox,

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:13.546
you gave each other tattoos.
-Mm-hmm.

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:15.615
-Now, obviously, you've received

00:05:15.615 --> 00:05:17.049
a fair amount of tattoos
over the years.

00:05:17.049 --> 00:05:20.419
Do you feel like you are
a good tattoo artist?

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:22.822
-Her skin's really so--

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:25.625
I felt that I --
Hers is kind of fading.

00:05:25.625 --> 00:05:29.161
-Okay.
-Her on me, though, she dug it

00:05:29.161 --> 00:05:31.197
in so deep that I think --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:34.967
-Oh, hers is fading because you
felt -- you felt for her.

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:36.869
Oh, you were very soft.
-And with mine, she was like,

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:39.071
"Oh, no, this is sticking."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.071 --> 00:05:44.010
Yeah. No, we did get our
voodoo dolls tattooed on us.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.646
-Oh, that's pretty good.
-Yeah.

00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:49.182
Yeah, I mean, you know, it's
interesting 'cause we were

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:54.853
watching the "Pam and Tommy"
series.

00:05:54.853 --> 00:05:58.491
I forgot that Mark Mahoney did
theirs, but Mark also did ours.

00:05:58.491 --> 00:06:00.025
-Oh, you have the same tattoo
artist?

00:06:00.025 --> 00:06:01.293
-Mm-hmm.
-Oh, that's pretty good.

00:06:01.293 --> 00:06:03.396
-Hopefully don't end up
the same.

00:06:03.396 --> 00:06:05.498
[ Laughter ]

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:08.668
Hopefully don't take after
all the paths that...

00:06:08.668 --> 00:06:10.736
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.736 --> 00:06:13.105
-I feel like he's due
a winner at this point.

00:06:13.105 --> 00:06:15.341
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:17.677
Do you remember any of --
You know, in watching

00:06:17.677 --> 00:06:20.713
the documentary, do you have
early rap lyrics,

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:23.015
like the first ones
you remember writing?

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:25.217
-Uh...

00:06:25.217 --> 00:06:26.752
Yeah, but you know what?

00:06:26.752 --> 00:06:30.223
You know when you're -- You know
when you're 13 and corny?

00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:31.758
-Yeah.

00:06:31.758 --> 00:06:34.993
-Yeah, like, I remember there
was -- I think there was one

00:06:34.993 --> 00:06:37.163
where I like -- You know
how you know it's corny?

00:06:37.163 --> 00:06:38.897
'Cause I used the word
Bud Light.

00:06:38.897 --> 00:06:42.134
And you're like 13. You're also
like, "You've never --"

00:06:42.134 --> 00:06:44.036
-You're like, "I know what
the coolest drink is."

00:06:44.036 --> 00:06:45.505
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, yeah.

00:06:45.505 --> 00:06:47.339
Yeah, yeah, yeah. It's so funny.

00:06:47.339 --> 00:06:49.709
There's no mention of, like,
cool liquors or anything.

00:06:49.709 --> 00:06:51.177
Like, "break out the Bud Light."

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:53.112
I don't know, dude, I don't
know. I just -- I remember that

00:06:53.112 --> 00:06:54.980
being that, and I remember
seeing that notebook,

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:57.116
and I burned it and I was like,
"No one will ever know

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:59.318
that I've written
this terrible rhyme."

00:06:59.318 --> 00:07:00.920
-Hey, man, it's always such
a pleasure to see you.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:01.987
-Thanks, Seth.
-Congratulations on everything

00:07:01.987 --> 00:07:03.588
and take care of yourself,
alright?

00:07:03.588 --> 00:07:05.090
No more --
-I will.

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:08.027
-Thank you, my friend. You guys,
that's Machine Gun Kelly.

00:07:08.027 --> 00:07:10.729
"Machine Gun Kelly's Life in
Pink" is streaming now on Hulu.

00:07:10.729 --> 00:07:12.365
We'll be right back
with Ingrid Andress.

